  "description": "COHDEK crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C51 H48 Dy4 N10 O18,2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.455-3.991 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 81.07-127.24°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C51H51Dy4N10O20. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
